| Tool                     | Basic Understanding (5–6 Lines)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      | Common Commands                                                                                     |
| ------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Nmap**                 | Network scanning and reconnaissance tool. Used to discover live hosts, open ports, running services, and operating systems. Essential for information gathering during penetration testing. Supports TCP, UDP, version detection, and vulnerability scanning scripts. One of the most important tools in Kali Linux. | `nmap <IP>`<br>`nmap -sV <IP>`<br>`nmap -O <IP>`<br>`nmap -A <IP>`<br>`nmap -p 1-1000 <IP>`         |
| **Netcat (nc)**          | Known as the "Swiss Army Knife" of networking. Used for port scanning, banner grabbing, file transfer, and creating TCP/UDP connections. Often used for troubleshooting and security testing. Can also create reverse and bind shells in controlled lab environments.                                                | `nc <IP> <PORT>`<br>`nc -lvnp 4444`<br>`nc -zv <IP> 1-1000`<br>`nc -u <IP> <PORT>`                  |
| **Wireshark**            | Network protocol analyzer used to capture and inspect packets. Helps understand network traffic and troubleshoot communication issues. Widely used in network forensics and security investigations. Provides a graphical interface for packet analysis.                                                             | `wireshark`<br>`wireshark &`                                                                        |
| **tcpdump**              | Command-line packet capture tool. Useful when GUI access is unavailable. Captures and analyzes network traffic in real time. Often used on servers and during incident response.                                                                                                                                     | `tcpdump -i eth0`<br>`tcpdump -n`<br>`tcpdump host <IP>`<br>`tcpdump port 80`                       |
| **Nikto**                | Web server vulnerability scanner. Detects outdated software, dangerous files, and misconfigurations. Useful during web application reconnaissance. Generates detailed security reports.                                                                                                                              | `nikto -h <IP>`<br>`nikto -h https://target.com`                                                    |
| **Dirb**                 | Web content discovery tool. Searches hidden directories and files on web servers. Helps identify admin panels, backups, and sensitive resources. Uses wordlists for brute-force directory discovery.                                                                                                                 | `dirb http://target.com`<br>`dirb http://target.com wordlist.txt`                                   |
| **Gobuster**             | Fast directory, DNS, and virtual host brute-forcing tool. Commonly used in web application penetration testing. Efficient and widely used by security professionals.                                                                                                                                                 | `gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt`<br>`gobuster dns -d domain.com -w wordlist.txt` |
| **Hydra**                | Password auditing and login brute-force tool. Supports SSH, FTP, HTTP, RDP, SMB, and many protocols. Used for testing password strength in authorized environments.                                                                                                                                                  | `hydra -l admin -P passwords.txt ssh://<IP>`<br>`hydra -L users.txt -P pass.txt ftp://<IP>`         |
| **John the Ripper**      | Password hash cracking tool. Supports many hash formats. Used to test password security and identify weak passwords. Commonly used after obtaining password hashes during assessments.                                                                                                                               | `john hashes.txt`<br>`john --wordlist=rockyou.txt hashes.txt`<br>`john --show hashes.txt`           |
| **Hashcat**              | Advanced password recovery and hash cracking tool. Supports CPU and GPU acceleration. Extremely fast and supports numerous hash types. Used for password auditing.                                                                                                                                                   | `hashcat -m 0 hash.txt wordlist.txt`<br>`hashcat --help`                                            |
| **Metasploit Framework** | Penetration testing framework used for exploitation, payload generation, and post-exploitation tasks. Contains thousands of modules for testing vulnerabilities. One of the most powerful tools in Kali Linux.                                                                                                       | `msfconsole`<br>`search exploit`<br>`use exploit/...`<br>`show options`<br>`run`                    |
| **Burp Suite**           | Web application security testing platform. Intercepts HTTP/HTTPS traffic between browser and server. Used for vulnerability assessment, request manipulation, and web testing.                                                                                                                                       | `burpsuite`                                                                                         |
| **SQLMap**               | Automated SQL Injection testing tool. Detects and exploits SQL injection vulnerabilities during authorized security assessments. Supports database fingerprinting and enumeration.                                                                                                                                   | `sqlmap -u "http://site.com?id=1"`<br>`sqlmap --dbs -u URL`                                         |
| **Aircrack-ng**          | Wireless security auditing suite. Used for Wi-Fi monitoring, packet capture, and security testing of wireless networks. Common tool for learning wireless security concepts.                                                                                                                                         | `airmon-ng start wlan0`<br>`airodump-ng wlan0mon`<br>`aircrack-ng capture.cap`                      |
| **Searchsploit**         | Offline exploit database search tool. Searches known public exploits stored locally. Useful for identifying available exploit code related to software versions.                                                                                                                                                     | `searchsploit apache`<br>`searchsploit smb`<br>`searchsploit -m <ID>`                               |
| **Whois**                | Retrieves domain registration and ownership information. Helpful during reconnaissance and OSINT activities. Provides registrar, nameserver, and registration details.                                                                                                                                               | `whois domain.com`                                                                                  |
| **Dig**                  | DNS lookup and troubleshooting tool. Queries DNS records such as A, MX, NS, and TXT. Useful for network reconnaissance and DNS analysis.                                                                                                                                                                             | `dig domain.com`<br>`dig MX domain.com`<br>`dig ANY domain.com`                                     |
| **Nslookup**             | Simple DNS query tool used to resolve domain names and obtain DNS records. Commonly used for troubleshooting DNS issues.                                                                                                                                                                                             | `nslookup domain.com`<br>`nslookup <IP>`                                                            |
| **theHarvester**         | OSINT information-gathering tool. Collects emails, subdomains, hosts, and employee information from public sources. Useful during reconnaissance phases.                                                                                                                                                             | `theHarvester -d domain.com -b google`                                                              |
| **Recon-ng**             | Reconnaissance framework for OSINT gathering. Automates information collection from multiple public sources. Useful for structured intelligence gathering.                                                                                                                                                           | `recon-ng`<br>`marketplace search`<br>`workspaces create lab`                                       |


| Command                 | Purpose                    |
| ----------------------- | -------------------------- |
| `pwd`                   | Show current directory     |
| `ls -la`                | List files and permissions |
| `cd <dir>`              | Change directory           |
| `mkdir test`            | Create directory           |
| `cp file1 file2`        | Copy file                  |
| `mv file1 file2`        | Move/Rename file           |
| `rm file`               | Delete file                |
| `cat file.txt`          | Display file content       |
| `grep word file.txt`    | Search text                |
| `chmod 755 file`        | Change permissions         |
| `sudo command`          | Run as administrator       |
| `ifconfig`              | View network interfaces    |
| `ip a`                  | Show IP addresses          |
| `ping <IP>`             | Check connectivity         |
| `netstat -tulnp`        | View listening ports       |
| `ss -tulnp`             | Display socket statistics  |
| `traceroute <IP>`       | Trace network path         |
| `history`               | Show command history       |
| `man command`           | Open manual page           |
| `apt update`            | Update package list        |
| `apt install <package>` | Install software           |
